{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1017102-gameline-as-private-military-company","id":1017102,"title":"Gameline As: Private Military Company","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-14T09:11:12-08:00","id":1017102,"title":"Gameline As: Private Military Company","content":"So, with Hurt Locker out, why don't we look at how each game-line would set up a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Private_military_company\" target=\"_blank\">PMC</a> composed of themselves (and their allies/associates)?<br /> <br /> Werewolves (with their Packs) and Sin-Eaters (with their Krewes) would fit right in the culture/industry, Vampires would need to keep to night operations (and/or leverage Ghouls in numbers), and as far a Mummies go, it would really be more their cult than them - unless the need were dire.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T09:18:13-08:00","id":1017105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1017102-gameline-as-private-military-company#post1017102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires would need to keep to night operations (and/or leverage Ghouls in numbers)</div> </div> </div> </div>Could get a lot of loyalty by going after veterans with otherwise incurable diseases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T09:36:19-08:00","id":1017109,"title":"","content":"Would mummies even have the numbers to support a PMC? I was under the impression that they're quite rare (like, only a thousand or two total). Same goes for Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Also: what's the incentive for these supernaturals to start a PMC? The reason for it would probably determine how it's structured in most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12761-suzuki","name":"Suzuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:12:21-08:00","id":1017130,"title":"","content":"A mummy could just be the power behind it, the PMC itself would be a cult, rather than a PMC made up of mummies.<br /> <br /> For vampires it would be political power and sway, as well as money and a use of their powers. Further from that it would depend on the individual in charge. Members of a bloodline like the Brothers of Ypres might do it to gain access to those poisoned by chemical warfare, members of the Ordo Dracul could do so in order to just get access to specimens who would otherwise go missing.<br /> <br /> Werewolves would have it as a pack structure. There's already Uratha in the defense industry, having one in a PMC, even if it is just an executive role, could change the whole thing into a pack. The benefits of not just a roaming pack, but a pack that is able to access areas far and wide, are great. You have more access to wolf-blooded and stranger spirits, you can have a reason to be poking into strange things and providing security to others. As effective mercenaries you would also have justification for the sacred hunt. Even if it wasn't the 'target' of your hire, you would easily be able to entwine your blood and your bone, your life and werewolf-side. A lodge could easily be formed out of a PMC, either as some sort of mercenary cult or a group of bale hounds offering up to Mammon and Thurifuge. Alternatively they could be a more standard Forsaken lodge, attempting to build another pillar out of service to one of the Firstborn. Even the Ivory Claws of the Pure could justify operating a PMC.<br /> <br /> The first werewolf game I ran operated with a pack as a PMC, but it was a small one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:43:58-08:00","id":1017147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suzuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1017102-gameline-as-private-military-company?p=1017109#post1017109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would mummies even have the numbers to support a PMC? I was under the impression that they're quite rare (like, only a thousand or two total). Same goes for Prometheans.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make it harder for those groups, yes. But I'd be interested in hearing about ways around those limitations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Suzuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1017102-gameline-as-private-military-company?p=1017109#post1017109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: what's the incentive for these supernaturals to start a PMC? The reason for it would probably determine how it's structured in most cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>What incentives can you see? The thread framing is each group as a PMC - but what forms would that take, why might they do such, what impact would their particular talents have, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:05:44-08:00","id":1017156,"title":"","content":"I think that it would be a lot more interesting to have a Werewolf Protectorate as a PMC than a Pack, though a Lodge would also be interesting in terms of divided loyalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:18:58-08:00","id":1017165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1017102-gameline-as-private-military-company?p=1017156#post1017156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it would be a lot more interesting to have a Werewolf Protectorate as a PMC than a Pack</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what you mean, but I think just by definition it wouldn't really work well as a protectorate, which is a coming together of packs or territories. I suppose you could hire on packs, but a PMC is obliged to go where the business is, rather than do what they want, so you wouldn't have the unity that a protectorate would have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:23:43-08:00","id":1017170,"title":"","content":"How would a Throng operate? I'd think there would a disproportionate number in the Soldier Role, and they probably wouldn't have very high numbers. And unlikely to get hired for bodyguard jobs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:30:30-08:00","id":1017178,"title":"","content":"I suppose they'd be good for when someone wants to cause chaos and destruction at a place. Just set them to guarding some building there and let the wasteland come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T15:46:11-08:00","id":1017361,"title":"","content":"Werewolves can already work as extremely well functioning squads. Prometheans could get a lot of good experience from being in a trade like that as well, even if it is a bit transitory as they come and go. In areas where there is war or PMCs heavily operate you already get people as myths and symbols. Most people aren't going to bat an eye when locals are claiming &quot;the devil appeared and destroyed the village single handedly!&quot; So in a way, it might be really... freeing for a lot of supernaturals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5761-shadowjakkal","name":"ShadowJakkal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T17:50:42-08:00","id":1018278,"title":"","content":"This reminds me that I have a work-in-progress for a hunter group outfitted as a PMC (who I see as the ugly, ugly bastard-child of Task Force Valkyrie and Ashwood Abby)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T05:39:54-08:00","id":1018431,"title":"","content":"That is terrifying on several levels.<br /> <br /> Well TFV undoubtedly uses the PMC role as a cover for when they need to place their people in an active combat area and can't slip them in as a government agent. I'm sure that the other conspiracies use the same trick as well, if only to move their people to where they're needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T12:26:45-08:00","id":1018544,"title":"","content":"I had a character that was making a miltary-style mercenary company that would include any and all supernatural creatures. Never got very far in that campaign but I've been writhing them up once they are fully operational for use in other campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}